    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. **Leading**: Player to dealer's left leads to first trick. Any card may be led.\n2. **Following Suit**: If a non-trump is led, players with that suit must either follow suit OR play a trump. A non-trump of a different suit can only be played if the player has no cards of the led suit.\n3. **Trumping Rules**: When playing a trump on a non-trump lead, it must be higher than any trumps already played to the trick. A lower trump can only be played if the player has no option (hand consists entirely of lower trumps).\n4. **Trump Led**: If a trump is led, other players must play trumps if they have them. Any trump may be played - no requirement to play higher.\n5. **Winning Tricks**: Highest trump wins, or if no trumps, highest card of led suit. Winner leads to next trick.",
    Player: "1. **Leading**: Player to dealer's left leads to first trick. Any card may be led.\n2. **Following Suit**: If a non-trump is led, players with that suit must either follow suit OR play a trump. A non-trump of a different suit can only be played if the player has no cards of the led suit.\n3. **Trumping Rules**: When playing a trump on a non-trump lead, it must be higher than any trumps already played to the trick. A lower trump can only be played if the player has no option (hand consists entirely of lower trumps).\n4. **Trump Led**: If a trump is led, other players must play trumps if they have them. Any trump may be played - no requirement to play higher.\n5. **Winning Tricks**: Highest trump wins, or if no trumps, highest card of led suit. Winner leads to next trick.",
    objective: 'Win tricks containing high-value cards. Score game points by reaching point thresholds with your partner.',
    gameplay: "1. **Leading**: Player to dealer's left leads to first trick. Any card may be led.\n2. **Following Suit**: If a non-trump is led, players with that suit must either follow suit OR play a trump. A non-trump of a different suit can only be played if the player has no cards of the led suit.\n3. **Trumping Rules**: When playing a trump on a non-trump lead, it must be higher than any trumps already played to the trick. A lower trump can only be played if the player has no option (hand consists entirely of lower trumps).\n4. **Trump Led**: If a trump is led, other players must play trumps if they have them. Any trump may be played - no requirement to play higher.\n5. **Winning Tricks**: Highest trump wins, or if no trumps, highest card of led suit. Winner leads to next trick.",
    keyRules: [
      'Trump Jack is worth 20 points, Trump Nine is worth 14 points',
      'Last trick is worth 5 points',
      'Total points per deal: 146',
      'Need 100+ card points to score 2 game points',
      'Win all tricks to score 5 game points',
    ],
